{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b0a838fb491aea35","name":"card_unit_p37los","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/units/card_unit_p37los","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"PZL.37 ŁOŚ","text":"When a friendly Polish air unit is destroyed, add a random Polish exile card to hand.","flavorText":"The PZL.37 Łoś was a Polish twin engined medium bomber that was first introduced to service in 1938. When it was first introduced it was considered to be one of the most advanced operational bombers in the world. At the start of WWII the Polish air force had 86 PZL.37’s in their service, but less than half of those were operational, some were in maintenance, others were being held in reserve or used for training purposes. The PZL’s that were operational managed to inflict considerable damage upon advancing German columns, but many were lost in combat due to lack of fighter protection. By 1940 many of the PZL’s had been evacuated to Romania where they were later seized by the Romanian government and used by the Romanian Air Force against the Allies. Over 120 PZL.37 Łoś were manufactured from 1938-1939, including variants. No PZL.37 Łoś aircraft remain today.","faction":"Poland","type":"bomber","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":2,"attack":2,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"moveReason_Destroyed":"CardMoveReason::NewEnumerator11","Name":"card_unit_p37los","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_p37los_title","SourceString":"PZL.37 ŁOŚ","LocalizedString":"PZL.37 ŁOŚ"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":2,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_p37los_text","SourceString":"When a friendly Polish air unit is destroyed, add a random Polish exile card to hand.","LocalizedString":"When a friendly Polish air unit is destroyed, add a random Polish exile card to hand."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_p37los_history","SourceString":"The PZL.37 Łoś was a Polish twin engined medium bomber that was first introduced to service in 1938. When it was first introduced it was considered to be one of the most advanced operational bombers in the world. At the start of WWII the Polish air force had 86 PZL.37’s in their service, but less than half of those were operational, some were in maintenance, others were being held in reserve or used for training purposes. The PZL’s that were operational managed to inflict considerable damage upon advancing German columns, but many were lost in combat due to lack of fighter protection. By 1940 many of the PZL’s had been evacuated to Romania where they were later seized by the Romanian government and used by the Romanian Air Force against the Allies. Over 120 PZL.37 Łoś were manufactured from 1938-1939, including variants. No PZL.37 Łoś aircraft remain today.","LocalizedString":"The PZL.37 Łoś was a Polish twin engined medium bomber that was first introduced to service in 1938. When it was first introduced it was considered to be one of the most advanced operational bombers in the world. At the start of WWII the Polish air force had 86 PZL.37’s in their service, but less than half of those were operational, some were in maintenance, others were being held in reserve or used for training purposes. The PZL’s that were operational managed to inflict considerable damage upon advancing German columns, but many were lost in combat due to lack of fighter protection. By 1940 many of the PZL’s had been evacuated to Romania where they were later seized by the Romanian government and used by the Romanian Air Force against the Allies. Over 120 PZL.37 Łoś were manufactured from 1938-1939, including variants. No PZL.37 Łoś aircraft remain today."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isReserved":true,"showBoostIcon":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDe